> Wanted to make sure as there was talk of different tests going on

For now I only have one template test case:
```cpp
CHECK(Math::division_round_up((T)0, (T)64) == 0);
CHECK(Math::division_round_up((T)63, (T)64) == 1);
CHECK(Math::division_round_up((T)64, (T)64) == 1);
CHECK(Math::division_round_up((T)65, (T)64) == 2);
```

All of them pass without any issue

> ```c++
> CHECK(Math::division_round_up((T)0, (T)64) == 0);
> CHECK(Math::division_round_up((T)63, (T)64) == 1);
> CHECK(Math::division_round_up((T)64, (T)64) == 1);
> CHECK(Math::division_round_up((T)65, (T)64) == 2);
> ```
> 
> All of them pass without any issue

Are the signed versions supposed to be used with negative `num` too? If yes, add some negative number tests. 

As adding tests is cheap, I would suggest adding:

> ```c++
> CHECK(Math::division_round_up((T)1, (T)64) == 1);
> ```

just to make sure there are no surprising off-by-one errors near zero. Also some tests where `p_den` is 1 would be nice.
